<%# The same Kith, with the web's furniture taken off.

    No masthead: the shell draws the navigation, and a second row of links
    under a native one is how an app announces it is a website in a coat.

    No safe-area padding either. `pt-safe` leaves with the masthead, and the
    bottom inset is already paid by the container the shell puts this web view
    in — `pb-safe` here would pay it twice and leave a gap under every screen.
    `pb-10` is what `pb-safe` resolves to off a phone, which is the spacing the
    reading column was designed with.

    Nothing else differs. If a screen ever needs more than this, that is a
    signal the web version of it is wrong. %>
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <%= render "layouts/head" %>
  </head>

  <body class="min-h-screen bg-paper text-ink antialiased">
    <main class="mx-auto w-full max-w-2xl px-5 pt-10 pb-10">
      <%= render "shared/flash" %>
      <%= yield %>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
